= Online platform =

== Overview ==
An '''online platform''' is a digital service that provides a shared technical and governance environment in which users, organizations, software, content, or transactions can interact.

Platforms often mediate discovery, identity, communication, publishing, exchange, ranking, or transactions. Their behavior emerges from software architecture together with policies, governance, incentives, moderation, and participant behavior.

An online platform is not the Internet itself and need not own the underlying network infrastructure.

== Boundaries ==
* online platform ≠ Internet
* platform ≠ protocol
* platform rules ≠ technical protocol rules

